[00:10.02] Ten years ago on a cool dark night
[00:16.32] There was someone killed 'neath the town hall light
[00:22.77] There were few at the scene and they all did agree
[00:30.06] That the man who ran looked a lot like me
[00:37.24] The judge said "Son, what is your alibi?
[00:44.56] If you were somewhere else then you won't have to die"
[00:51.71] I spoke not a word although it meant my life
[00:59.06] I had been in the arms of my best friend's wife
[01:05.38] She walks these hills in a long black veil
[01:15.36] She visits my grave where the night winds wail
[01:24.45] Nobody knows, no, and nobody sees
[01:31.73] Nobody knows but me
[01:40.84] The scaffold was high and eternity neared
[01:51.70] She stood in the crowd and shed not a tear
[01:58.98] But sometimes at night when the cold wind moans
[02:05.34] In a long black veil she cries over my bones
[02:23.59] 